{"id":"data-reading-charts","title":"Data science: reading charts","subject":"Data science","label":"Data science","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":171,"duration":171.35,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":485,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Opening","start":0,"end":15.285},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":15.285,"end":49.465},{"id":"explain2","title":"Read and mislead","start":49.465,"end":90.825},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":90.825,"end":112.915},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":112.915,"end":121.925},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":121.925,"end":125.595},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Mistakes","start":125.595,"end":151.865},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":151.865,"end":171.35}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":7.67,"text":"Here's a puzzle. Two sales bars show ninety-eight and one hundred. One bar looks twice as tall as the other. How can that be?","w":[0.5,0.9,1.01,1.47,1.69,2.04,2.32,2.61,3.35,3.57,3.8,4.31,4.54,4.77,5.11,5.45,5.62,5.91,6.08,6.3,6.7,6.93,7.16,7.44]},{"s":0,"a":8.12,"b":14.86,"text":"I'm Kora, and today you'll learn to read charts without being fooled. By the end, you'll pick the right chart and spot the trick.","w":[8.22,8.4,9.18,9.3,9.6,9.82,10.04,10.18,10.42,10.78,11.1,11.38,12.28,12.46,12.64,12.8,13.04,13.24,13.36,13.6,14.04,14.22,14.5,14.62]},{"s":1,"a":15.71,"b":19.47,"text":"A chart turns a table into a picture, so you can see a pattern quickly.","w":[15.76,15.9,16.22,16.54,16.6,16.92,17.16,17.26,17.96,18.12,18.26,18.42,18.6,18.68,19.1]},{"s":1,"a":19.77,"b":23.59,"text":"A chart is not decoration. It is a tool for honest comparison.","w":[19.82,19.96,20.34,20.52,20.74,21.82,21.92,22.06,22.14,22.44,22.64,22.98]},{"s":1,"a":23.89,"b":27.88,"text":"Choose by job. A bar chart compares amounts between categories.","w":[23.94,24.26,24.48,25.26,25.34,25.6,25.92,26.38,26.72,27.1]},{"s":1,"a":28.18,"b":30.39,"text":"A line chart shows change over time.","w":[28.26,28.4,28.72,29.08,29.42,29.8,30.02]},{"s":1,"a":30.69,"b":36.58,"text":"A pie chart shows parts of one whole. Use it only with a few slices that add up to one hundred percent.","w":[30.76,30.86,31.14,31.44,31.78,32.12,32.4,32.6,33.44,33.6,33.78,34,34.14,34.22,34.46,34.9,35.14,35.32,35.44,35.66,35.8,36.1]},{"s":1,"a":36.88,"b":43.33,"text":"A histogram shows how one numerical variable is spread out, in ranges called bins. Its bars touch.","w":[36.92,37,37.6,37.92,38.22,38.4,38.92,39.52,39.62,40.02,40.56,40.7,41.2,41.5,42.32,42.5,42.9]},{"s":1,"a":43.63,"b":49.04,"text":"A scatter plot shows the relationship between two numerical variables, with one dot per record.","w":[43.7,43.8,44.18,44.52,44.86,44.98,45.62,46,46.24,46.74,47.58,47.94,48.16,48.44,48.64]},{"s":2,"a":49.89,"b":56.38,"text":"To read any chart, go in order. First the title. Then the axes: what each one measures, and its units.","w":[49.92,50.06,50.28,50.48,51.2,51.36,51.48,52.24,52.58,52.72,53.28,53.46,53.68,54.48,54.74,55,55.16,55.64,55.76,55.94]},{"s":2,"a":56.68,"b":64.26,"text":"Next the scale: where it starts and how big the steps are. Then the legend or key, then the source and date.","w":[56.76,57.08,57.22,58.18,58.42,58.56,59.04,59.22,59.48,59.72,59.84,60.26,61.2,61.44,61.58,62,62.18,62.88,63.16,63.34,63.78,63.92]},{"s":2,"a":64.56,"b":69.31,"text":"Only then read the pattern: highest, lowest, trend, anything unusual.","w":[64.66,64.96,65.22,65.4,65.5,66.26,66.96,67.56,68.4,68.82]},{"s":2,"a":69.61,"b":78.02,"text":"Charts can mislead. A bar axis that does not start at zero makes a small difference look huge. That is called a truncated axis.","w":[69.68,70.06,70.24,71.18,71.26,71.64,72,72.14,72.36,72.62,72.92,73.04,73.46,73.7,73.82,74.16,74.88,75.12,76.04,76.32,76.44,76.8,76.9,77.52]},{"s":2,"a":78.32,"b":87.95,"text":"Uneven steps on an axis mislead too. So do hand-picked dates that hide the longer trend, three-dimensional effects that distort sizes, and charts with no source.","w":[78.32,78.74,79.09,79.27,79.45,79.75,80.22,80.52,80.7,80.88,81.59,81.95,82.24,82.54,82.78,83.19,83.61,84.68,85.16,85.45,85.93,86.34,86.58,87,87.3,87.47]},{"s":2,"a":88.25,"b":90.4,"text":"The scale is often where the tricks hide.","w":[88.28,88.46,88.86,89.08,89.34,89.52,89.68,89.98]},{"s":3,"a":91.25,"b":95.14,"text":"Back to our puzzle. Two bars show sales of ninety-eight and one hundred.","w":[91.25,91.52,91.68,91.89,92.32,92.53,92.8,93.06,93.38,93.54,94.23,94.45,94.66]},{"s":3,"a":95.44,"b":100.8,"text":"On an axis that starts at ninety-six, the first bar rises only two units, and the second rises four.","w":[95.44,95.6,95.76,96.02,96.29,96.66,96.82,97.46,97.67,97.99,98.2,98.52,98.78,99,99.37,99.58,99.79,100.16,100.48]},{"s":3,"a":101.1,"b":106.05,"text":"So the taller bar looks twice as tall, though the real difference is only about two percent.","w":[101.2,101.34,101.48,101.88,102.14,102.42,102.78,102.9,103.52,103.72,103.9,104.24,104.74,104.94,105.18,105.5,105.7]},{"s":3,"a":106.35,"b":109.47,"text":"The values are close. The picture exaggerates them.","w":[106.36,106.52,107,107.14,107.98,108.12,108.52,109.18]},{"s":3,"a":109.77,"b":112.49,"text":"So always check the scale before you judge the size.","w":[109.84,110.08,110.44,110.68,110.82,111.2,111.48,111.66,111.94,112.06]},{"s":4,"a":113.34,"b":118.81,"text":"You want to show how a city's temperature changed over twelve months. Which chart would you use, and why?","w":[113.36,113.5,113.68,113.8,114.04,114.26,114.36,114.74,115.24,115.72,115.94,116.3,117.14,117.42,117.66,117.82,118.06,118.38,118.52]},{"s":4,"a":119.26,"b":121.5,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[119.28,119.6,119.84,119.96,120.26,120.94,121.14]},{"s":5,"a":122.35,"b":125.17,"text":"A line chart, because it shows change over time.","w":[122.44,122.56,122.86,123.52,123.8,123.94,124.34,124.68,124.88]},{"s":6,"a":126.02,"b":133.06,"text":"One mistake is reading the picture before the axes. Avoid it by reading the title, the axes and the scale first.","w":[126.2,126.34,126.9,127.06,127.36,127.48,127.84,128.16,128.38,129.4,129.8,129.92,130.12,130.4,130.52,131.38,131.64,132.06,132.18,132.3,132.64]},{"s":6,"a":133.36,"b":139.28,"text":"Another is using a pie chart for things that are not parts of one whole. Save pie charts for parts of one whole.","w":[133.44,133.82,133.98,134.22,134.3,134.58,134.88,135.08,135.32,135.48,135.62,135.84,136.12,136.3,136.48,137.48,137.78,138.02,138.3,138.46,138.72,138.88,139.02]},{"s":6,"a":139.58,"b":143.34,"text":"And do not compare charts with different scales. Compare like with like.","w":[139.6,139.76,139.94,140.18,140.58,140.96,141.18,141.54,142.32,142.76,142.98,143.18]},{"s":6,"a":143.64,"b":151.44,"text":"Finally, do not confuse a histogram with a bar chart. Histogram bars touch and show bins. Bar chart bars usually have gaps.","w":[143.7,144.18,144.36,144.56,145.06,145.14,145.64,145.78,145.86,146.1,146.82,147.34,147.72,148.04,148.2,148.44,149.48,149.74,150.02,150.38,150.72,150.92]},{"s":7,"a":152.29,"b":154.06,"text":"Choose the chart that fits the job.","w":[152.36,152.68,152.84,153.14,153.34,153.6,153.74]},{"s":7,"a":154.36,"b":158.83,"text":"Read the title, axes, scale, key and source before the pattern.","w":[154.4,154.6,154.72,155.68,156.52,157.1,157.48,157.66,158.04,158.34,158.42]},{"s":7,"a":159.13,"b":161.92,"text":"Check the scale before trusting any difference.","w":[159.22,159.52,159.66,160.1,160.46,161.1,161.32]},{"s":7,"a":162.22,"b":167.33,"text":"Top tip: when a chart surprises you, look again at the axis and the source.","w":[162.26,162.58,163.32,163.52,163.64,163.98,164.52,165.14,165.38,165.76,165.86,166.1,166.6,166.72,166.84]},{"s":7,"a":167.63,"b":170.75,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and charts will become clear.","w":[167.64,167.88,168.4,168.62,169.48,169.66,170,170.16,170.46]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Opening puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Bars: 98 and 100; one looks twice as tall"},{"at":8.02,"kind":"term","text":"Chart literacy","detail":"Read charts without being fooled; pick the right chart and spot tricks"}]},{"at":15.46,"heading":"Chart basics","items":[{"at":15.61,"kind":"text","text":"Chart: table → picture; see pattern quickly"},{"at":19.67,"kind":"term","text":"Honest comparison","detail":"A chart is a tool, not decoration"}]},{"at":23.64,"heading":"Choose by job","items":[{"at":23.79,"kind":"term","text":"Bar chart","detail":"Compares amounts between categories"},{"at":28.08,"kind":"term","text":"Line chart","detail":"Shows change over time"},{"at":30.59,"kind":"term","text":"Pie chart","detail":"Parts of one whole; few slices; add to 100%"},{"at":36.78,"kind":"term","text":"Histogram","detail":"One numerical variable spread in bins; bars touch"},{"at":43.53,"kind":"term","text":"Scatter plot","detail":"Relationship between two numerical variables; one dot per record"}]},{"at":49.64,"heading":"Read in order","items":[{"at":49.79,"kind":"text","text":"1 Title; 2 axes: measures and units"},{"at":56.58,"kind":"text","text":"3 Scale: start and step size; 4 key; 5 source and date"},{"at":64.46,"kind":"text","text":"Then pattern: highest, lowest, trend, unusual"}]},{"at":69.36,"heading":"How charts mislead","items":[{"at":69.51,"kind":"term","text":"Truncated axis","detail":"Bar axis not starting at zero; small difference looks huge"},{"at":69.51,"kind":"image","text":"An axis that starts at 9,100: small differences look big","src":"truncated.webp","credit":"Smallman12q · CC0 · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":78.22,"kind":"text","text":"Also: uneven steps, hand-picked dates, 3D effects, no source"},{"at":88.15,"kind":"tip","text":"The scale is often where tricks hide"}]},{"at":91,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":91.15,"kind":"text","text":"Sales: 98 and 100"},{"at":95.34,"kind":"formula","text":"98 − 96 = 2; 100 − 96 = 4"},{"at":101,"kind":"text","text":"Taller bar looks 2×; real difference about 2%"},{"at":106.25,"kind":"text","text":"Values are close; picture exaggerates"},{"at":106.25,"kind":"image","text":"The same data with the axis starting at 0","src":"full.webp","credit":"Smallman12q · CC0 · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":109.67,"kind":"tip","text":"Always check the scale before judging size"}]},{"at":112.92,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":112.92,"kind":"question","text":"You want to show how a city's temperature changed over twelve months. Which chart would you use, and why?"}]},{"at":122.1,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":122.25,"kind":"term","text":"Line chart","detail":"Shows change over time"},{"at":122.25,"kind":"text","text":"Use for temperature over 12 months"}]},{"at":125.77,"heading":"Mistakes","items":[{"at":125.92,"kind":"wrong","text":"Reading picture before axes"},{"at":125.92,"kind":"right","text":"Read title, axes and scale first"},{"at":133.26,"kind":"wrong","text":"Pie chart for things that are not parts of a whole"},{"at":133.26,"kind":"right","text":"Save pie charts for parts of one whole"}]},{"at":139.33,"heading":"Mistakes","items":[{"at":139.48,"kind":"wrong","text":"Comparing charts with different scales"},{"at":139.48,"kind":"right","text":"Compare like with like"},{"at":143.54,"kind":"wrong","text":"Confusing histogram with bar chart"},{"at":143.54,"kind":"right","text":"Histogram bars touch, show bins; bar chart bars have gaps"}]},{"at":152.04,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":152.19,"kind":"text","text":"Choose the chart that fits the job."},{"at":154.26,"kind":"text","text":"Title, axes, scale, key, source; then the pattern"},{"at":159.03,"kind":"text","text":"Check the scale before trusting a difference"},{"at":162.12,"kind":"tip","text":"When a chart surprises you, look again at the axis and the source"}]}],"check":{"at":121.75,"seconds":10,"question":"You want to show how a city's temperature changed over twelve months. Which chart would you use, and why?","answer":"A line chart, because it shows change over time."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[{"title":"Truncated Bar Graph.svg","author":"Smallman12q","licence":"CC0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Truncated_Bar_Graph.svg"},{"title":"Bar graph.svg","author":"Smallman12q","licence":"CC0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bar_graph.svg"}],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}